The mumps add-on is an interface to the MUMPS package. The MUMPS package
contains a sparse direct solver and can be compiled in two ways:
  - sequential version, which is a free alternative for MA41 and MA57.
  - parallel version using MPI.

Directions for the installation of the MUMPS package are given in the
README.mumps file in the install folder in the root of tfem.

Note: compilation of the add-on requires the MUMPS package to be installed.

Usage
=====

Please read the manual of MUMPS first. (Read at least chapters 1,2,3 and 10).
Read the source of mumps.f90 to see how it is composed.

A simple main program will look like

  program myprog

  ...

  use mumps_m

  ...

  type(dmumps_struc) :: mumps_par

  ...

! start mpi

  call mpi_init(ierr)

! create mumps_par structure

  call create ( mumps_par )

! build matrix on the host

  if ( mumps_par%myid == 0 ) then

    ... ( build matrix on the host )

  end if

! solve on all processors

  call solve_system_mumps ( sysmatrix, rhsd, sol, mumps_par )

! delete all data for building the matrix

  if ( mumps_par%myid == 0 ) then

    ... ( delete all data )

  end if

! delete mumps_par structure

  call delete ( mumps_par )

! stop mpi

  call mpi_finalize(ierr)

  end program myprog


Remarks
=======

For sequential use, the mpi calls are not needed.

To run a program which was build with MPI the following command must be issued

  mpirun -n X example

where X is the number of cores. If OpenMP is also used it is recommended to set
OMP_NUM_THREADS by the command

  export OMP_NUM_THREADS = Y

such that, X*Y < number of cores, otherwise performance might be seriously
compromised.
